.TH CRC16 1 "November 2026" "crc16 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
crc16 \- compute many CRC\-16 variants of a file in a single pass
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crc16
.RI [ OPTION ]...\&
.RI [ FILE ]...\&
.br
.B crc16 \-\-list
.br
.B crc16 \-\-self\-test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B crc16
reads each
.I FILE
once and prints the CRC\-16 of its contents for 31 standard variants, or for
the subset chosen with
.BR \-a .
With no
.IR FILE ,
or when
.I FILE
is
.BR \- ,
it reads standard input.
.PP
Variants follow the Rocksoft/RevEng parameter model (width 16, polynomial,
initial value, input and output reflection, final XOR) and the names of the
.UR https://reveng.sourceforge.io/crc\-catalogue/16.htm
RevEng CRC catalogue
.UE .
Every supported variant reflects its input and output identically, which the
program relies on.
.PP
The default text output reproduces that of the reference script
.I crc16.py
bit for bit, except that the first line is in English.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-algorithm " \fINAME\fP"
Select one or more variants.
The option may be repeated and
.I NAME
may be a comma\-separated list.
Names are case\-insensitive, may be written with or without the
.B CRC\-16/
prefix, and may be any alias listed under
.BR ALGORITHMS .
Results are printed in the order given, without duplicates.
The default is all variants.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List every variant with its polynomial, initial value, reflection, final XOR,
check value and aliases, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " \fIFMT\fP"
Output format:
.BR text " (default), " csv ", " tsv " or " json .
See
.BR "OUTPUT FORMATS" .
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-lowercase
Print hexadecimal digits in lowercase.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Omit the
.B Processed N bytes.
line (text format only).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " \fIN\fP"
Number of worker threads.
.B 0
(the default) uses one per online CPU,
.B 1
disables threading; the maximum is 1024.
Threads are started only for inputs of at least 4\ MiB.
The result never depends on this setting.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mmap
Read files with
.BR fread (3)
instead of mapping them into memory.
By default, regular files of at least 4\ MiB are mapped with
.BR mmap (2)
on platforms that have it; pipes, standard input and smaller files are
always read.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
Compute every variant over the ASCII string
.B 123456789
and compare it with the published check value.
Also run a 64\ KiB pseudo\-random buffer through the fast paths used on this
machine (carry\-less multiply, worker threads as set by
.BR \-j )
and compare the result with a bit\-by\-bit reference.
Prints one line per variant (only failures with
.BR \-q )
and exits 0 if all agree, 1 otherwise.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display the version and the minimum ISO C standard, and exit.
.PP
A lone
.B \-\-
ends option processing.
Long options must be spelled in full.
.SH ALGORITHMS
All values are in normal form, and names are shown without the
.B CRC\-16/
prefix.
.B Check
is the CRC of the ASCII string
.BR 123456789 .
Reflection applies to both input and output.
.PP
